<p class="lesson-lead">Everything starts here: fork the starter, clone it, and take a character from zero to a moving, animated sprite. The three habits this unit builds — read before you run, predict before you change, tune one number at a time — carry through the entire year.</p>

<h2>Lessons</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>ID</th><th>Title</th><th>What you build / learn</th></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/1.1a.html">1.1a</a></td><td>Launch: Fork, Clone &amp; Press Play</td><td>from GitHub fork to a running build on your machine</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/1.2a.html">1.2a</a></td><td>The Unity Editor Tour</td><td>Hierarchy, Inspector, Scene, Play — the four windows you live in</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/1.3a.html">1.3a</a></td><td>Your First Script: Variables &amp; Update</td><td>fields, Start vs Update, Debug.Log as your eyes</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/1.4a.html">1.4a</a></td><td>Movement I: Input, Direction, Vector</td><td>GetAxis → direction → vector → Translate</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/1.5a.html">1.5a</a></td><td>Movement II: Speed, deltaTime &amp; Tuning</td><td>frame-rate independence and the live-tuning workflow</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/1.6a.html">1.6a</a></td><td>Animation States: IsWalking, WalkDir, Attack</td><td>animator parameters driven by code</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Concepts this unit owns</h2>
<p>This unit owns the <strong>movement pattern</strong> — input, direction, speed, deltaTime, Translate — that every controller in the starter uses, and the <strong>predict–change–verify</strong> habit every lesson after it assumes. CED: CRD-1 (program development), AAP-2 (managing complexity with variables).</p>

